## Test Anti-Pattern Audit: `ProductCatalogTests.cs`

**Framework**: MSTest · **Tests**: 10 · **Production**: `ProductCatalog.cs`

### Summary

| Severity | Count |
|----------|-------|
| 🔴 Critical | 2 (systemic — affects all 10 tests) |
| 🟡 Medium | 1 |

This suite is the textbook **coverage-touching** anti-pattern. Every public method on `ProductCatalog` is called, which achieves high line-coverage, but **6 of 10 tests have zero assertions** and the remaining 4 only assert `IsNotNull`. No test verifies an actual business outcome. Every bug in `UpdatePrice`, `ApplyBulkDiscount`, `ImportFromCsv`, `Search`, `ExportToCsv`, or `RemoveProduct` will sail straight to production.

---

### 🔴 Critical #1 — No Assertions (6 tests)

These tests execute code and discard the result. They will pass even if the method is a no-op.

| Test method | Line | What it misses |
|---|---|---|
| `AddProduct_Works` | 17–21 | Never verifies the product was stored |
| `UpdatePrice_Works` | 32–36 | Never verifies the price actually changed |
| `RemoveProduct_Works` | 39–43 | Never verifies the product was deleted |
| `GetProductCount_Works` | 63–66 | Never checks the returned count |
| `ApplyBulkDiscount_Works` | 69–74 | Never checks prices were reduced |
| `ImportFromCsv_Works` | 85–88 | Never checks imported products exist or are correct |

**Example fix — `UpdatePrice_Works`:**

```csharp
// BEFORE (no assertion — always passes)
[TestMethod]
public void UpdatePrice_Works()
{
    _catalog.AddProduct(new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m));
    _catalog.UpdatePrice("SKU-001", 14.99m);
}

// AFTER (verifies the business outcome)
[TestMethod]
public void UpdatePrice_ChangesStoredPrice()
{
    _catalog.AddProduct(new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m));

    _catalog.UpdatePrice("SKU-001", 14.99m);

    var updated = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
    Assert.AreEqual(14.99m, updated!.Price);
}
```

**Example fix — `RemoveProduct_Works`:**

```csharp
// AFTER
[TestMethod]
public void RemoveProduct_MakesProductUnretrievable()
{
    _catalog.AddProduct(new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m));

    _catalog.RemoveProduct("SKU-001");

    Assert.IsNull(_catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001"));
}
```

**Example fix — `ApplyBulkDiscount_Works`:**

```csharp
// AFTER
[TestMethod]
public void ApplyBulkDiscount_ReducesAllPricesByFraction()
{
